Good old cron would probably be more than enough.

What *I'd* do (assuming I understood the requirements correctly):

- Have clients drop files in incoming/, with no possibility of
  overwriting each others' stuff.  Any way would do, e.g. old-fashioned
  anonymous ftp.

- Write a program 'merge-records -o master incoming/*' which moves all
  files from incoming, hunts through them for records not present in
  'master', and adds these to 'master'.  Could be generalized to add
  bones to a collection of bones, etc.

- Have cron run merge-records once a minute or so.

There are some problems left to solve there though:
- merge-records stealing things from incoming/ while they're still
  being written
- exposing 'master' for download while it's still being updated
- DOS attacks/spam by creating lots of phony data
  ("Cheap.V.i.a.g.r.a. killed by a succubus, while helpless"?)

